{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 32, :comments ["<b>But the wheat and the spelt were not struck.</b> Because it is about to say, 'and eat the remnant of what is left to you from the hail' — and there is an opening for a challenger to distinguish and say: was it not already stated, 'and all the grass of the field the hail struck'? Therefore it preempted and taught you here that the wheat and the spelt were not struck, כי אפילת הנה — for they were still dark (unripe), so that what the hail did not break, the locust consumed; the hail damages the hard (growth) and the locust eats the soft." "<b>For they were dark.</b> From the root אופל — for they were still in the ground and had not yet appeared above ground."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:56:47.183793097Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}